<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fold">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A fold is an arched (bent) tectonic structure caused by the ductile deformation of rocks.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="de">Eine Falte ist eine gewölbte (gebogene) tektonische Struktur, die durch die duktile Verformung von Gestein entstanden ist.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Un pli est une structure tectonique courbe (ployée) résultant d'une déformation ductile des roches.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="it">Una piega è una struttura tettonica arcuata (piegata) causata dalla deformazione duttile delle rocce.</skos:definition>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">fold</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Falte</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">pli</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">piega</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Antiform"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Synform"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Backfold"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Tectonic Structures</skos:prefLabel>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Antiform">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">An antiform is a fold with its convex side facing upward (n-shaped). If the stratigraphic sequence is normal (older strata in the core of the fold, surrounded resp. overlain by younger strata), the antiform is an anticline. If the sequence is inverted (younger strata in the core of the fold, surrounded resp. overlain by older strata), it is referred to as an inverted syncline.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Une antiforme est un pli dont la convexité (i.e. la courbure) est orientée vers le haut (en forme de n). Si la série est normale (couches plus jeunes au-dessus des couches plus anciennes), l'antiforme est un anticlinal. Si la série est inverse (couches plus jeunes en dessous des couches plus anciennes), on parlera d'une antiforme synclinale ou d'un synclinal retourné.</skos:definition>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">antiform</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Antiform</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">antiforme</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">antiforme</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fold"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Anticline"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/SynclineOverturned"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Synform">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A synform is a fold with its convex side facing downwards (u-shaped). If the stratigraphic sequence is normal (younger strata in the core of the fold, surrounded resp. underlain by older strata), the synform is a syncline. However, if the sequence is inverted (older strata in the core of the fold, surrounded resp.underlain by older strata), it is referred to as an inverted anticline.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Une synforme est un pli dont la convexité est orientée vers le bas (pli en forme de U). Si la série est normale (couches plus jeunes au-dessus des couches plus âgées), la synforme est un synclinal. Par contre, si la série est inverse (couches plus récentes sous les couches plus anciennes), on parlera d'une synforme anticlinale ou d'un anticlinal retourné.</skos:definition>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">synform</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Synform</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">synforme</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">sinforme</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fold"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Syncline"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/AnticlineOverturned"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

