<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/BerisalFold">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Berisal Backfold is a synform on the northwestern side of the Lepontine Dome, with the Berisal Nappe and the Gälmji Zone in its core.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Lepontic</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="fr">synforme de Berisal (Jeanbourquin &amp; Burri 1989)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Berisal Backfold</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Berisal-Rückfalte</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Pli en retour de Berisal</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Retropiega di Berisal</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Berisal-Synform</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Berisal Synform</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Synforme de Berisal</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="it">Sinforme di Berisal</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="it">Piega retroflessa di Berisal</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Backfold"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/WandfluhhornFold">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Wandfluhhorn (TI) = Pizzo Bìela (Italia): coord. 2679000/1133000</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Alpe Bosa-Wandfluhhorn Fold (located between the Maggia and Antigorio valleys) is a multi-kilometer-scale isoclinal structure formed during a late phase of deformation.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="de">Grosse isoklinale Falte westlich des Maggia-Tales. Wurde früher als synklinale Verbindung zwischen Antigorio- und Monte-Leone-Decke betrachtet (Preiswerk 1921, Niggli et al. 1936). Später als "postnappe fold" neu interpretiert (Hunziker &amp; Wieland 1966, Della Torre et al. 2015).</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Lepontic</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Wandfluhhorn antiformal syncline = Wandfluhhorn transverse fold (Steck 2008)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="it">sinclinale del Wandfluhhorn (Della Torre &amp; Maggini 2015)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Wandfluhhorn Backfold</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Wandfluhhorn-Rückfalte</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Pli en retour du Wandfluhhorn</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Retropiega del Wandfluhhorn</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Alpe Bosa-Wandfluhhorn double fold</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="it">Piega retroflessa del Wandfluhhorn</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Backfold"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/ZiccherFold">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Monte Ziccer (Italia): coord. 2684600/1113000</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Ziccher Fold is a multi-kilometer-scale isoclinal structure formed during a late phase of deformation.</skos:definition>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Ziccher anticline (Steck 2008)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Ziccher Backfold</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Ziccher-Rückfalte</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Ziccher-Antiklinale</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Backfold"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/MischabelFold">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Mischabel Backfold is a large structure situated in the Zermatt Valley and further east. In its steep overturned flank, the Siviez-Mischabel Nappe is in contact with, from west to east, the Zermatt-Saas Fee Nappe, the Portjengrat Nappe and the Antrona Nappe.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Penninic</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="de">Mischabelfalte = Mischabelrückfalte (Müller 1983)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="it">strutture retroflesse del Mischabel (Dal Piaz et al. 1992)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Mischabel fold = Mischabel backfold (Steck et al. 2015)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="fr">pli en retour des Mischabelhörner = pli en retour de la Mischabel (Argand 1911b)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Mischabel Backfold</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Mischabel-Rückfalte</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Pli en retour des Mischabel</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Retropiega delle Mischabel</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="it">Piega retroflessa delle Mischabel</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Backfold"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/NiemetBeverinFold">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Niemet-Beverin Backfold is a very large-scale north facing structure that postdates nappe stacking of the Eastern Penninic and can be followed all the way into the Prättigau Half-Window (e.g., Schmid et al. 1990, Schreurs 1995, Weh &amp; Froitzheim 2001). The sedimentary Schams Nappe Complex and the upper part of the Lower Penninic Tomül Nappe are wrapped around the Suretta Nappe in this mega-fold and backthrust to the southeast in an overturned position over the top of the Suretta Nappe and of the Upper Penninic Avers Nappe.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Graubünden</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="de">Niemet-Beverin-Falte (Wyss &amp; Wiederkehr 2017)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Niemet-Beverin Backfold</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Niemet-Beverin-Rückfalte</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Pli en retour de Niemet-Beverin</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Retropiega di Niemet-Beverin</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="it">Piega retroflessa di Niemet-Beverin</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Backfold"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A tectonic accident (resp. a fault in a broad sense) is a tectonic structure resulting from a brittle deformation (fracture) accompanied by relative opposite movement on either side of the structure. It consists of a plane or zone of rupture along which two compartments move relative to one another.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="de">Eine tektonische Störung (bzw. ein Bruch im weiteren Sinne) ist eine spröde tektonische Struktur, die mit einer relativen Bewegung in entgegengesetzte Richtungen auf beiden Seiten der Struktur einhergeht. Sie besteht aus einer Bruchfläche oder einer Bruchzone, entlang derer sich zwei Teile relativ zueinander verschieben.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Un accident tectonique (resp. une faille au sens large) est une structure tectonique résultant d'une déformation cassante (fracture) accompagnée d'un déplacement relatif des compartiments situés de part et d'autre. Elle consiste en un plan ou une zone de rupture le long de laquelle deux blocs rocheux se déplacent l'un par rapport à l'autre.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="it">Una faglia (in senso lato) è una struttura tettonica risultante da una deformazione a rottura (frattura) accompagnata da uno spostamento relativo dei compartimenti situati su entrambi i lati. Consiste in un piano o in una zona di rottura lungo la quale due blocchi rocciosi si spostano l'uno rispetto all'altro.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">The term "fault s.s." is sometimes restricted to steeply dipping structures, whereas the more generic term "(tectonic) accident" is used for any kinf of "faults s.l.".</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">tectonic accident</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">tektonische Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">accident tectonique</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">faglia</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">fault</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Bruch, Verwerfung</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">faille</skos:altLabel>
