<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/PeriadriaticFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Periadriatic Fault System is a complex lineament stretching from Hungary in the east, through Slovenia, Austria and Italy, to western Piemonte. This fault system marks a major tectonic boundary between the Southern Alps and the main body of the Alps to the north. 
In the area of the Tectonic Map of Switzerland, the Periadriatic Fault System is represented by its westernmost segments, from east to west: the Giudicarie Fault, the Tonale Fault and the Canavese Fault (the last two of which are sometimes groupes together as the “Insubric Fault”).</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Peri-Adriatic line, Periadriatische Naht (Bögel 1975), Periadriatic Lineament (Hoinkes &amp; Thöni 1993), lineamento Periadriatico (Dal Piaz et al. 1992a), Periadriatic Fault System = Periadriatic Shear Zone = Insubric mylonite belt (Babist et al. 2006), Periadriatic line (Steck 2008)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Periadriatic Fault System</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Periadriatische Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Système de failles périadriatique</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Periadriatic Lineament</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Periadriatische Linie</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Ligne Périadriatique</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="it">Lineamento Periadriatico</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/InsubricFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/GiudicarieFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/PustertalGailtalFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/KarawankenFault"/>
	<skos:narrowMatch rdf:resource="https://resource.geosphere.at/thes/fault/206"/>
	<skos:narrowMatch rdf:resource="https://voc.europe-geology.eu/hike/faults/493"/>
	<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://voc.europe-geology.eu/hike/faults/494"/>
	<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://resource.geosphere.at/thes/fault/205"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/MontaltoDoraFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Montalto (Italia)</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Discontinuité tectonique ductile (mylonites) développée sous faciès prehnite-pumpellyite-actinote au bord méridional (= interne) de la zone du Canavese s.s.. Elle sépare cette dernière de la zone d'Ivrée (à faciès granulitique). Son âge est plus ancien que la ligne externe du Canavese (segment SW de la ligne insubrienne).</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Montalto-Dora Fault ("Internal Canavese Fault") is a ductile tectonic discontinuity (mylonitic zone) developed under prehnite-pumpellyite-actinote metamorphic facies at the southern boundary of the Canavese Zone. It separates the latter from the Ivrea Zone (with granulite metamorphic facies). It is older than the northern boundary of the Canavese Zone (south-western segment of the Insubric Fault).</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine &gt; Canavese</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Internal Canavese Line = ICL (Biino &amp; Compagnoni 1989)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="it">linea Montalto Dora = linea del Canavese interna (Dal Piaz et al. 1992a)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Internal Canavese Line = ligne Interne du Canavèse (Borghi et al. 1996)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">internal Canavese line = ICL (Ferrando et al. 2004)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Montalto-Dora Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Montalto-Dora-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille de Montalto-Dora</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia di Montalto-Dora</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Internal Canavese Fault</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille Interne du Canavese</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia Interna del Canavese</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<skos:related rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/CanaveseFault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/FaultNormal">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A fault is described as normal when the compartment above the fault (the ‘roof’) moves downwards relative to the compartment below the fault (the ‘wall’). This is typical of extensional settings, such as passive margins, rift systems or oceanic ridges.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Une faille est dite normale lorsque le compartiment situé au-dessus de la faille ("toit") descend par rapport au compartiment situé en dessous de la faille ("mur"). Typique des contextes d'extension (étirement), comme les marges passives, les rifts ou les dorsales océaniques.</skos:definition>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">normal fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">faille normale</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">faglia normale</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="it">faglia diretta</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">faille distensive</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">faille divergente</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/AostaRanzolaFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/BadenIrchelHerdernFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/SchwarzwaldFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/NeuhausenFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/FreiburgBonndorfBodenseeFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/RandenFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/SchienerBergFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/BachliGiesenenFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/PejoFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/LuganoMonteGronaValGrandeFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Detachment"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/SimplonFault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/WehrHaerkingenFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Wehr-Härkingen Line is a NE-SW trending fault separating the Eastern Rhenish Jura from the Easternmost Jura.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Jura</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Wehr-Härkingen Line</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Wehr-Härkingen-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille Wehr-Härkingen</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia Wehr-Härkingen</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/StGallenFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The St. Gallen Fault is presently considered active (Heuberger et al. 2016).</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Bodensee</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">St. Gallen Fault (Heuberger et al. 2016, Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">St. Gallen Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">St.-Gallen-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille de St-Gall</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/SaxSchwendeFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Sax-Schwende Fault is an important N–S oriented fault between Sax and Appenzell that has been active during the internal deformation of the Säntis Nappe.</skos:definition>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Sax-Schwende Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Sax-Schwende-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia Sax-Schwende</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/ForcolaFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The ENE-dipping Forcola Fault partially delimits the structural Lepontine Dome to the southeast (symmetrically to the Simplon Fault). It represents a late structure belonging to a penetrative orogen-parallel ductile shear zone.</skos:definition>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Forcola Fault (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Forcola Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Forcola-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia della Forcola</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille de la Forcola</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
	<dct:source>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</dct:source>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</dct:bibliographicCitation>
	<skos:scope>Lepontine Dome</skos:scope>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/ColDeBardFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">West of Aosta, the Col de Bard Fault can be considered as the continuation of the Aosta-Ranzola Fault progressively flattening towards a more moderate NW-  dipping fault as it progressively bends into a NW–  SE strike, which offset mainly the Middle Penninic units (Gouffon 1993, Gouffon &amp; Burri 1997). Alternatively, Malusà et al. (2009) consider the Col de Bard Fault as the termination of the Cogne Fault Zone.</skos:definition>
	<skos:example xml:lang="fr">accident col de Bard - Saint-Nicolas (Gouffon 1993)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Col de Bard Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Col-de-Bard-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille du Col de Bard</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia del Col de Bard</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<skos:related rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/CogneFault"/>
	<skos:related rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/AostaRanzolaFault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
	<dct:source>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</dct:source>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Malusà M.G., Polino R., Zattin M. (2009): Strain partitioning in the axial NW Alps since the Oligocene. Tectonics 28/3, TC3005</dct:bibliographicCitation>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Y. (1993): Géologie de la nappe du Grand St-Bernard entre la Doire Baltée et la frontière suisse (Vallée d’Aoste – Italie). Mém. Géol. (Lausanne) 12</dct:bibliographicCitation>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Y. (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</dct:bibliographicCitation>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Y., Burri M. (1997): Les nappes des Pontis, de Siviez-Mischabel et du Mont Fort dans les vallées de Bagnes, d’Entremont (Valais, Suisse) et d’Aoste (Italie). – Eclogae geol. Helv. 90/1, 29-41</dct:bibliographicCitation>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/CogneFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:example xml:lang="fr">Faisceau de Cogne (Elter 1972, Sartori 1990)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="it">fascio di Cogne (Dal Piaz et al. 1992a)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Cogne Fault Zone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Cogne-Störungszone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Zone de failles de Cogne</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Zona di faglie di Cogne</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</dct:bibliographicCitation>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Malusà M.G., Polino R., Zattin M. (2009): Strain partitioning in the axial NW Alps since the Oligocene. Tectonics 28/3, TC3005</dct:bibliographicCitation>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/BellefaceTrajoFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Belleface-Trajo Fault (situated between the Savara and Cogne valleys) is a steeply dipping, NE-SW-oriented deformation zone of the Grand Paradis Massif, separating the Grivola Unit (to its SE) from the Zona Interne (to its NW).</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Zone de déformation NE-SW raide située entre le Valsavrenche de la vallée de Cogne, séparant l'unité de la Grivola au SE de la Zona Interna au NW.</skos:definition>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Belleface-Trajo fault (Malusà et al. 2005)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Belleface-Trajo Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Belleface-Trajo-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille de Belleface-Trajo</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia di Belleface-Trajo</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:notation>BTF</skos:notation>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Malusà Ma.G., Polino R., Martin S. (2005): The Gran San Bernardo nappe in the Aosta valley (western Alps): a composite stack of distinct continental crust units. Bull. Soc. géol. Fr. 176/5, 417-431</dct:bibliographicCitation>
	<skos:scope>Middle Penninice</skos:scope>
	<skos:scope>Vallée d'Aoste</skos:scope>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/GalloFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Val del Gallo (GR)/(Italia), coord. 2812850/1167115</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Gallo Fault is a steeply dipping fault separating the S-charl Nappe and the Umbrail-Chavalatsch Slices, resp. the Quattervals Nappe.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="de">Steilstehende tektonische Grenzfläche zwischen S-charl-Decke und Umbrail-Chavalatsch-Schuppen bzw. Quattervals-Decke.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Austroalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:scopeNote>Punt dal Gall, Val Mora, obere Val Vau, Nordwand des Piz Lad, Punt Teal</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="de">Gallo-Linie (Karagounis 1962, Schmid 1973)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Gallo Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Gallo-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille du Gallo</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia del Gallo</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Gallo Line</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Gallo-Linie</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">From its geographical description, the Gallo Fault In HIKE (4615) and Geosphere Thesaurus (173) seems to correspond to the Trupchun-Braulio Fault of lexic !</skos:editorialNote>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
	<dct:source>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</dct:source>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</dct:bibliographicCitation>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/LeccoFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Lecco (Italia)</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Lecco Fault is a NW–SE trending structure separating the sediments of the former Generoso Basin from the Upper Orobic Nappe of the Bergamasc Alps. It is probably a reactivated Mesozoic fault.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Lecco Fault (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Lecco Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Lecco-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille de Lecco</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia di Lecco</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
	<dct:source>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</dct:source>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</dct:bibliographicCitation>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/LagoMaggioreFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Lago Maggiore (Italia), coord. 2689195/1084485</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Lago Maggiore Fault marks the boundary between the Ivrea-Ceneri Complex and the Upper Orobic Nappe. It was originally an Early Mesozoic rift fault that separated the Early Jurassic Monte Nudo Basin in the east from the Gozzano High in the west.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Lago Maggiore Fault (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Lago Maggiore Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Lago-Maggiore-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille du Lago Maggiore</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia del Lago Maggiore</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille du Lac Majeur</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
	<dct:source>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</dct:source>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</dct:bibliographicCitation>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/CossatoMergozzoBrissagoFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Cossato-Mergozzo-Brissago Fault separates the Ivrea Zone from the Strona-Ceneri Zone. It is interpreted as a Permian fault zone due to its association with Permian granites and its later cutting by the Pogallo Fault.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="it">linea di Cossago/Cossato-Mergozzo-Brissago (Dal Piaz et al. 1992a)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Cossato-Mergozzo-Brissago Fault = CMB (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Cossato-Mergozzo-Brissago Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Cossato-Mergozzo-Brissago-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia di Cossato-Mergozzo-Brissago</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille de Cossato-Mergozzo-Brissago</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:notation>CMB</skos:notation>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
	<dct:source>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</dct:source>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</dct:bibliographicCitation>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/CremosinaFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The WSW–ENE trending Cremosina Fault is a major structure cutting the Ivrea-Ceneri Complex south of the Lago d’Orta, with Early Jurassic sediments trapped along it.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Cremosina Fault (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="it">linea della Cremosina (Dal Piaz et al. 1992a)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Cremosina Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Cremosina-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille de la Cremosina</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia della Cremosina</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
	<dct:source>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</dct:source>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</dct:bibliographicCitation>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/ValCollaFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Late Variscan Val Colla Fault is a mylonitic fault zone separating the Strona-Ceneri and Val Colla zones and sealed at M. Caslano, west of Lugano, by unconformably overlying Permian volcanics. In the northeast, the Val Colla Fault is cut by Alpine faults and interrupted by the Tonale Fault.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Val Colla Fault (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Val Colla Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Val-Colla-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille du Val Colla</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia della Val Colla</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/MarzioFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Marzio Fault separates the WSW–ENE trending Arbostora Anticline (southern part of the Varesotto Imbricates) from a complex syncline of imbricated Mesozoic sediments.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine &gt; Varesotto</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Marzio Fault (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Marzio Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Marzio-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille de Marzio</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia di Marzio</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
	<dct:source>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</dct:source>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</dct:bibliographicCitation>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/BallinoFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Ballino (Italia), coord. 2861390/1096015</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:member rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/FaultSynsedimentary"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Ballino Fault is an important N–S trending transfer fault north of Lago di Garda. It is a reactivated and inverted Mesozoic extensional fault which coincides with the facies change between the Mesozoic Lombardian Basin and the Trento Plateau.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicUnits/SouthAlpine"/>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Ballino Fault (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Ballino Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Ballino-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille de Ballino</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia di Ballino</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
	<dct:source>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</dct:source>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Castellarin A. (1972): Evoluzione paleotettonica sinsedimentaria del limite tra Piattaforma veneta e Bacino Lombardo a nord di Riva del Garda. G. Geol. (Bologna) 2/38, 11– 212</dct:bibliographicCitation>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Y., (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500'000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</dct:bibliographicCitation>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/SabionFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Sabion Fault is a small ramp anticline situated east of the Giudicarie fault and probably reactivating a Permian–Mesozoic structural high.</skos:definition>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Sabion Fault (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Sabion Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Sabion-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille de Sabion</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia di Sabion</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/FaultStrikeSlip">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A fault is described as a strike-slip fault when it results primarily from horizontal sliding along a generally subvertical plane. This type of fault is caused by shear stress. Strike-slip faults can be dextral or sinistral, depending on whether the block opposite the observer moves to the right or to the left (respectively).</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Une faille est dite décrochante lorsqu'elle résulte essentiellement d'un mouvement de coulissage horizontal le long d'un plan généralement subvertical. Ce type de faille est la conséquence de contraintes cisaillantes. Les décrochements peuvent être dextres ou sénestres, suivant que le compartiment opposé à l'observateur se déplace vers la droite ou la gauche (respectivement).</skos:definition>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">strike-slip fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Transversalstörung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">faille décrochante</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">décrochement, faille transverse</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/FaultStrikeSlipSinistral"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/FaultStrikeSlipDextral"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/BellefontaineFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/CaquerelleFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/MorezFault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/SoyhieresFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The NE-SW trending Sohyières Fault separates the Ferrette Block (to the West) from the Blauen Block (to the East).</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">swissJura3D</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Sohyières Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Soyhières-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille de Soyhières</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia di Soyhières</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/WoelfinswilFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The NNE-SSW trending Wölfinswil Fault consitutes the western boundary of the Bözberg and Urgiz Blocks.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">swissJura3D</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Wölfinswil Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Wölfinswil-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille de Wölfinswil</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia di Wölfinswil</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/RuetilochFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The NE-SW trending Rütlioch Fault separates the Balsthal Block and the Ramiswil Block, connecting the Hornegg Thrust and the Mümliswil Thrust.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">swissJura3D</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Rütiloch Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Rütiloch-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille du Rütiloch</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia del Rütiloch</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/WisnerhoechiFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The NE-SW trending Wisnerhöchi Fault separates the Ramiswil Block and the Balsthal Block, connecting the Mümliswil Thrust and the Gugen Thrust.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">swissJura3D</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Wisnerhöchi Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Wisnerhöchi-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille du Wisnerhöchi</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia del Wisnerhöchi</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/FaultComposite">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">fault with a composite movement (i.e. both vertical and horizontal)</skos:definition>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">composite fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">faille composite</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/RhoneSimplonFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/EngadineFault"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/RoteKuhGampelFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Rote Kuh-Gampel Shear Zone is a reactivated paleofault separating the External Aar Massif to the north-west from the Internal Aar Massif to the south-east.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Helvetic</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="fr">faille Rote Kuh-Gampel (Burkhard 1988)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="de">Rote-Kuh-Gampel-Verwerfung (Dolivo 1982)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="de">Roti-Chüe-Gampel-Scherzone (Sartori et al. 2017)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Jurassic Rote Kuh - Gampel normal fault (Krayenbühl &amp; Steck 2009)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Rote Kuh-Gampel fault (Steck et al. 2015)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Rote Kuh-Gampel Shear Zone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Rote-Kuh-Gampel-Scherzone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Zone de cisaillement de Rote Kuh-Gampel</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Zona di taglio di Rote Kuh.Gampel</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Roti-Chüe-Gampel-Scherzone</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Roti Chüe-Gampel Shear Zone</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Zone de cisaillement de la Roti Chüe-Gampel</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel>Zona di taglia della Roti Chüe-Gampel</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/ZoneShear"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/StellihornFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Stellihorn (VS): coord. 2643535/1098460</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Stellihorn Shear Zone separates the basement of the Monte Rosa Nappe into two parts.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="de">Alpine Scherzone am nördlichen Rand der Monte-Rosa-Decke.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Penninic</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="it">Zona dello Stelli = zona di shear dello Stelli (Dal Piaz et al. 1992)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="de">Stelli-Zone (Bearth 1952, Bearth 1957b)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Stellihorn shear zone (Pleuger et al. 2008)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Stellihorn shear zone = Stelli mylonite zone (Steck et al. 2015)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Stellihorn Shear Zone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Stellihorn-Scherzone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Zone de cisaillement du Stellihorn</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Zona di taglio dello Stellihorn</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Stelli-Zone</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="it">Zona di taglio dello Stelli</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/ZoneShear"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/ArcegnoPalanzenoFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Arcegno (TI): coord. 2700735/1113175</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Arcegno-Palanzeno Shear Zone (Burri 2005) is situated in the E-W striking “root zone” of the Penninic and Lepontic nappes (Southern Steep Belt; Milnes 1974 b) and was later overprinted by the Centovalli Fault.</skos:definition>
	<skos:example xml:lang="de">Südliche Gneis- und Schieferzone = Zone von Arcegno (Kern 1947)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="de">Zone von Arcegno (Forster 1947, Walter 1950, Paraskevopoulos 1953, Kobe 1956)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Arcegno-Palanzeno Shear Zone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Arcegno-Palanzeno-Scherzone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Zone de cisaillement d'Arcegno-Palanzeno</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Zona di taglio d'Arcegno-Palanzeno</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Arcegno Zone</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">This zone is rather a tectono-stratigraphic unit (strongly deformed gneiss and schist of the Sesia Nappe).</skos:editorialNote>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/ZoneShear"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/FaultReverse">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">A fault is described as reverse when the compartment above the fault (the ‘roof’) rises relative to the compartment below the fault (the ‘wall’). This is typical of compressional settings (shortening), such as collision zones (mountain chains) and subduction zones. A low-angle reverse fault is a thrust fault.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Une faille est dite inverse lorsque le compartiment situé au-dessus de la faille ("toit") monte par rapport au compartiment situé en dessous de la faille ("mur"). Caractéristique des contextes de compression (raccourcissement), comme les zones de collision (montagnes) et de subduction. Une faille inverse à faible angle est un chevauchement.</skos:definition>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">reverse fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">faille inverse</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">faglia inversa</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">faille compressive, faille convergente</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Fault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Thrust"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/InsubricFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The term of “Insubric Fault” designates the Tonale and Canavese faults, which accommodate dextral slip motion and/or backthrusting of the nappe stack north of these faults over the South Alpine domain. The ductile fault rocks (mylonites) found along the Insubric Fault primarily formed during the Oligocene (32–23 Ma; Schmid et al. 1989), while the brittle component observed along the Tonale Fault is considerably younger (Müller et al. 2002, Pleuger et al. 2012).</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="it">Complesso sistema di miloniti e cataclasiti che separa tettonicamente le unità Pennidi ed Austridi dal basamento Sudalpino.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Linea Insubrica (Godenzi 1963, Sciesa 1991), Insubrian line, Insubric fault, Insubrische Linie, Insubric fault = Insubrische Störung = faille insubrienne (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Insubric Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Insubrische Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille Insubrienne</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia Insubrica</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Insubrische Linie</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Ligne Insubrienne</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="it">Linea Insubrica</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Tonale-Canavese Fault System</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="en">Insubrian Line</skos:hiddenLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/PeriadriaticFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/CanaveseFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TonaleFault"/>
	<skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="https://voc.europe-geology.eu/hike/faults/4620"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/GiudicarieFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Giudicarie Fault represents a NNE- SSW oriented segment of the Periadriatic Fault System.. It separates two E-W segments of this Periadriatic Fault System: the Tonale Fault in the west and the Pustertal-Gailtal Fault in the east, which are offset by about 75 km. The southern part of the Giudicarie Fault is entirely located in the South Alpine, while the northern part separates Austroalpine units to the west and South Alpine units to the east. Only the southern part occurs in the area of the map (SE border), with a small portion of the northern part occurring at the eastern edge of the map area.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">ligne judicarienne (Henny 1918), Judicarien-Linie, Giudicarie Fault = Giudicarie-Störung = Faille des Giudicarie (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Giudicarie Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Giudicarie-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille des Giudicarie</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia delle Giudicarie</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Judikarien-Linie</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Ligne judicarienne</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="it">Linea delle Giudicarie</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/PeriadriaticFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/GiudicarieSouthFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/GiudicarieNorthFault"/>
	<skos:relatedMatch rdf:resource="https://voc.europe-geology.eu/hike/faults/4623"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/PustertalGailtalFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Pustertal-Gailtal Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Pustertal-Gailtal-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille du Pustertal-Gailtal</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia della Pusteria-Gailtal</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/PeriadriaticFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/PustertalFault"/>
	<skos:narrower rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/GailtalFault"/>
	<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://resource.geosphere.at/thes/fault/164"/>
	<skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://voc.europe-geology.eu/hike/faults/495"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/KarawankenFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">linea delle Karawanken (Dal Piaz et al. 1992a)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Karawanken Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Karawanken-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Karawanken-Linie</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/PeriadriaticFault"/>
	<skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="https://resource.geosphere.at/thes/fault/163"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/CanaveseFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Discontinuité tectonique cassante développée au bord septentrional (= externe) de la zone du Canavese s.s. Elle sépare cette dernière de la zone de Sesia. En direction du nord-est, la zone du Canavese se pince et la ligne du Canavese rejoint alors la terminaison sud-occidentale de la ligne insubrienne entre la zone d'Ivrée à métamorphisme granulitique anté-alpin et la nappe de Sesia à métamorphisme éclogitique alpin.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The (External) Canavese Fault is a major tectonic discontinuity developed along the northern boundary of the Canavese Zone. It separates the latter from the Sesia Nappe. Towards the north-east, the Canavese Zone gets narrower and the Canavese Fault then joins the south-western tip of the Insubric Fault between the Ivrea Zone (with pre-Alpine granulitic metamorphism) and the Sesia Nappe (with Alpine eclogitic metamorphism).</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">The "Internal Canavese Fault", bounding the Canavese Zone towards the southeast, at the contact with the Ivrea Zone, should rather be referred to as the Montalto-Dora Fault in order to avoid confusion with the (External) Canavese Zone.</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">xxx (Novarese 1929), South Canavese Line (Boriani &amp; Sacchi 1974), Ligne du Canavese (Steck &amp; Tièche 1976), External Canavese Line = ECL (Biino &amp; Compagnoni 1989), linea del Canavese (Dal Piaz et al. 1992a), External Canavese Line = ligne Externe du Canavèse (Borghi et al. 1996), external Canavese line = ECL = Canavese line s.s. (Ferrando et al. 2004), Canavese Fault = Canavese-Störung = Faille du Canavese (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Canavese Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Canavese-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille du Canavese</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia del Canavese</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">External Canavese Fault</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Canavese Line</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/InsubricFault"/>
	<skos:related rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/MontaltoDoraFault"/>
	<skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="https://voc.europe-geology.eu/hike/faults/4621"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TonaleFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Tonale Fault, formed by dextral shearing under ductile and later brittle conditions, is part of the Periadriatic Fault System. It separates the Austroalpine units of the Central Alps in the north from the South Alpine units in the south.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">faille du Tonale (Henny 1918), accident du Tonale, Jorio-Tonale, Iorio-Tonale-Linie = Insubriche Linie (Knoblauch &amp; Reinhard 1939), Tonale-Linie = Tonale-Störung (Büchi &amp; Trümpy 1976), Tonale-Centovalli (Boriani et al. 1990), Faglia del Tonale (Scesia 1991), Steilzone nördlich des Veltins ~ Tonale Linie (Spillmann 1993), Tonale Fault = Tonale-Störung = Faille du Tonale (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Tonale Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Tonale-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille du Tonale</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia del Tonale</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/InsubricFault"/>
	<skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="https://voc.europe-geology.eu/hike/faults/4622"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/PustertalFault">
