<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/AostaRanzolaFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The E -W trending Aosta-Ranzola Fault consists of a 1–2 km wide network of closely spaced and predominantly N-dipping normal faults that follow the Valle d’Aosta between Brusson and Aosta. The maximum cumulative vertical throw across this steeply N-dipping central part of the fault system exhuming the footwall located on the southern side of the valley amounts to some 3 km (Bistacchi et al. 2001). East of Brusson, this normal fault finds a rather abrupt end against the Ospizio-Sottile Fault. The Aosta-Ranzola Fault is of Oligocene age, as documented by the synkinematic emplacement of gold bearing quartz veins and calc-alkaline dykes dated at 29 Ma (Dal Piaz et al. 1979, Diamond &amp; Wiedenbeck 1986).</skos:definition>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Aosta fault (Steck et al. 2015)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Aosta-Ranzola Fault (Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="it">faglia oligocenico-neogenica Aosta-Colle di Joux-Ranzola = linea Aosta-Ranzola (Dal Piaz et al. 1992a)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Aosta-Ranzola extensional fault system (Bistacchi et al. 2001)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Aosta-Ranzola fault (Babist et al. 2006)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="fr">faille du val d'Aoste (Gouffon 1993)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Aosta-Ranzola Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Aosta-Ranzola-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille d'Aosta-Ranzola</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia di Aosta-Ranzola</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/FaultNormal"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
	<dct:source>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</dct:source>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Y. (1993): Géologie de la nappe du Grand St-Bernard entre la Doire Baltée et la frontière suisse (Vallée d’Aoste – Italie). Mém. Géol. (Lausanne) 12</dct:bibliographicCitation>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Y. (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</dct:bibliographicCitation>
	<dct:bibliographicCitation>Gouffon Y., Burri M. (1997): Les nappes des Pontis, de Siviez-Mischabel et du Mont Fort dans les vallées de Bagnes, d’Entremont (Valais, Suisse) et d’Aoste (Italie). – Eclogae geol. Helv. 90/1, 29-41</dct:bibliographicCitation>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/BadenIrchelHerdernFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Baden-Irchel-Herdern Lineament is is a Cenozoic normal fault situated north of the Lägern Anticline and coinciding with the southern boundary of the Late Paleozoic Constance-Frick Trough (Naef et al. 1995, Madritsch et al. 2018). It is compressively overprinted between Baden and Bülach resulting in a structurally complex, faisceaux-like fault zone only visible in seismic reflection profiles (Malz et al. 2016).</skos:definition>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Baden-Irchel-Herdern Lineament (Naef et al. 1995, Malz et al. 2016, Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Baden-Irchel-Herdern Lineament</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Baden-Irchel-Herdern-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille Baden-Irchel-Herdern</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia Baden-Irchel-Herdern</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Baden-Irchel-Herdern-Linie</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:notation xml:lang="en">BIH</skos:notation>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/FaultNormal"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/SchwarzwaldFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The NE-SW trending Schwarzwald Fault is a major (1st order) normal fault separating the Western and Eastern Rhenish Jura (and further to the north, the Upper Rhine Graben to the West from the South German Platform and in particular its basement, the Schwarzwald Massif to the East).</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">swissJura3D, Süddeutschland</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Schwarzwald Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Schwarzwald-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille du Schwarzwald</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia del Schwarzwald</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Schwarzwald Line, Black Forest Line</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Schwarzwald-Linie</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Accident de la Forêt Noir</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:notation xml:lang="en">SWL</skos:notation>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/FaultNormal"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/NeuhausenFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Neuhausen Fault marks the southwestern boundary of the NW–SE trending extensional Hegau-Bodensee Graben. It is situated in the southeastern extension of the Freiburg-Bonndorf-Bodensee Fault Zone.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Süddeutschland</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Neuhausen Fault</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Neuhausen-Störung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Faille de Neuhausen</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Faglia di Neuhausen</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Neuhausen Thrust</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/FaultNormal"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/FreiburgBonndorfBodenseeFault">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
