<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/MettauThrust">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The S-vergent Mettau Thrust is regarded as belonging to the South German Platform.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Jura</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Mettau Thrust</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Mettau-Überschiebung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Chevauchement de Mettau</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Sovrascorrimento di Mettau</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Mettau Overthrust</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Mettauer Überschiebung</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Thrust"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/ZebruThrust">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The WNW-ESE striking Zebrù Thrust bought the Ortler Nappe over the Campo and the Laas nappes during an early stage of Late Cretaceous WNW-  directed thrusting (Conti et al. 1994, Conti 1997). Over most of its strike, the Zebrù Thrust follows the incompetent sediments of the Raibl Group, which serve as the dominant basal décollement horizon for the Mesozoic sequence of the Ortler Nappe.</skos:definition>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="de">Westgerichtete Überschiebung (Conti 1991) zwischen Campo- und Ortler-Decke.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Austroalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Zebrù Thrust</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Zebrù-Überschiebung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Chevauchement du Zebrù</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Sovrascorrimento dello Zebrù</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Zebrù-Linie</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="it">Linea dello Zebrù</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Thrust"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/LaasThrust">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Laas Thrust (“Laaser Linie” of Mair et al. 2007) is a steeply S-dipping thrust separating a sliver of Mesozoic cover of the Laas Nappe from the Campo Nappe (the “Pejo-Einheit” of Mair et al. 2007).</skos:definition>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Laas Thrust</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Laas-Überschiebung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Chevauchement de Laas</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Sovrascorrimento di Laas</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Laaser Linie</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Thrust"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TrupchunBraulioThrust">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Trupchun-Braulio Thrust formed during a later stage of the Cretaceous orogeny. It juxtaposed the Quattervals Nappe (in the west) and the Umbrail-Terza Slice Complex (in the east) over the Ortler Nappe. The thrust is marked by calcite mylonites derived from the footwall and exhibits numerous top-WNW sense-of-shear indicators (Conti 1997).</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Austroalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Trupchun-Braulio Thrust</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Trupchun-Braulio-Überschiebung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Chevauchement de Trupchun-Braulio</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Sovrascorrimento di Trupchun-Braulio</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">
From its geographical description, the Gallo Fault In HIKE (4615) and Geosphere Thesaurus (173) seems to correspond to the Trupchun-Braulio Fault of lexic !</skos:editorialNote>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Thrust"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TamaroThrust">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Tamaro Thrust marks the boundary between the Ivrea-Ceneri Complex and the Upper Orobic Nappe.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Tamaro Thrust</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Tamaro-Überschiebung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Tamaro Fault</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Thrust"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/VillafortunaThrust">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Villaforuna Thrust is a S-vergent thrust forming, together with the Monte Olimpino Backthrust, a broad syncline in the subsurface of the Po Plain.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Southalpine</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Villafortuna Thrust</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Villafortuna-Überschiebung</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/Thrust"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

