<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TurbaZone">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Turba Shear Zone is a large normal fault separating the southernmost part of the Avers Nappe and the backthrust Schams and Tomül nappes in the footwall from the Platta and Malenco-Forno-Lizun nappes in the hangingwall.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Penninic</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Turba-Scherzone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Turba Shear Zone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Zone de cisaillement du Turba</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Zona di taglio del Turba</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="de">Turba-Mylonitzone</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Turba Normal Fault</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Turba Mylonitic Zone</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Zone mylonitique du Turba</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:altLabel xml:lang="it">Zona milonitica del Turba</skos:altLabel>
	<skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">"Shear Zone" for naming the tectonic structure (process), "Mylonite Zone" for naming the tectonic unit and "Mylonite" for naming the material (body of rock).</skos:changeNote>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/ZoneShear"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/VinschgauZone">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Vinschgau Shear Zone represents the structurally highest unit of the Campo Nappe Complex and constitutes a greenschist-facies Alpine mylonitic belt with a thickness of up to 2–3 km that accommodates W-  directed thrusting of the Ötztal Nappe Complex in the area north of the Vinschgau Valley floor (Schmid &amp; Haas 1989). South of the valley floor and in the lowermost Val Müstair, the same mylonitic belt accommodates WNW-  directed thrusting of the easternmost part of the Umbrail-Terza Slice Complex over the S-charl-Sesvenna Nappe (Conti 1997). The protoliths of this mylonitic belt include pre-Permian basement, sericite-rich Permo-Triassic siliciclastic metasediments and rare occurrences of mid-Triassic carbonates that are part of the Campo Nappe Complex. The fact that the Vinschgau Shear Zone directly overlies both the rest of the Campo Nappe Complex and the easternmost parts of the S-charl-Sesvenna Nappe shows that, at a large scale, the Campo Nappe Complex and the S-charl-Sesvenna Nappe occupy about the same tectonic position within the Upper Austroalpine nappe stack.</skos:definition>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Vinschgau Shear Zone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Vinschgau-Scherzone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Zone de cisaillement du Val Venosta</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Zona di Taglio della Val Venosta</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/ZoneShear"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/RoisanCignanaZone">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Gouffon Yves (Editor) (2024): Tectonic Map of Switzerland 1:500000, Explanatory notes. Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, Wabern</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:isDefinedBy>Roisan (Italia): coord. 2590160/1070375</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
	<rdfs:comment>https://data.geo.admin.ch/ch.swisstopo.geologie-tektonische_karte/pdf/Erl-TK500_2024.pdf</rdfs:comment>
	<skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Roisan-Cignana Shear Zone (Manzotti et al. 2014 a) is a strongly deformed mélange zone separating the Dent Blanche Nappe (below) from the Mont Mary Nappe (above). It The consists of slices of Mesozoic sediments and crystalline basement in a mylonitic matrix derived from the adjacent Dent Blanche Nappe (Arolla Unit) and of the Mont Mary Nappe (Lower and Upper units) (Manzotti et al. 2014a). The high-pressure mineral assemblages along the contact between these tectonic slices indicates that their emplacement occurred in an early deformation stage, before or during the subduction.</skos:definition>
	<skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Salassic</skos:scopeNote>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Roisan-Cignana Shear Zone (Manzotti &amp; Ballèvre 2017, Gouffon et al. 2024)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="it">Zona di Roisan (Dal Piaz et al. 1992a, Dal Piaz et al. 2015)</skos:example>
	<skos:example xml:lang="en">Roisan zone (Dal Piaz et al. 2015)</skos:example>
	<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/TectonicStructures"/>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Roisan-Cignana Shear Zone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Roisan-Cignana-Scherzone</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Zone de cisaillement de Roisan-Cignana</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Zona di taglio di Roisan-Cignana</skos:prefLabel>
	<skos:broader rdf:resource="https://lexic.swissgeol.ch/TectonicStructures/ZoneShear"/>
	<adms:status xml:lang="en">active</adms:status>
</rdf:Description>

